Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: qca8k: preserve QinQ bridge database domains

QinQ assigns each VLAN-unaware bridge a private VID using its DSA bridge
number. Without fdb_isolation, DSA zeroes that number in FDB/MDB database
notifications and the QinQ mapper programs VID 3072 instead of the active
bridge VID (3088 for bridge 1). Static unicast and multicast entries then
miss the packets they should constrain.

Advertise the isolation already provided by the private bridge VLANs.
This preserves database identity for both add/delete notifications and CPU
port reference counting. Standard QCA tagging retains its existing behavior.

--- a/drivers/net/dsa/qca/qca8k-qinq.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/qca/qca8k-qinq.c
@@ -761,6 +761,10 @@ int qca8k_qinq_setup(struct dsa_switch *ds)
 	if (ret)
 		goto fail;
 	ds->max_num_bridges = DSA_TAG_8021Q_MAX_NUM_BRIDGES;
+	/* Private bridge VIDs require the real database bridge number,
+	 * including FDB/MDB notifications and shared CPU-port entries.
+	 */
+	ds->fdb_isolation = true;
 	ds->needs_standalone_vlan_filtering = true;
 	ds->configure_vlan_while_not_filtering = true;
 	rtnl_lock();
